  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available and is not used for billing purposes.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use SPP as a billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents advances from associated companies of $50,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $23,420,000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">We use RSGM for the amortization of (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes to customers. The deferred taxes associated with public utility plant property will be amortized over a period ranging from 45 to 60 years and deferred taxes not related to public utility property will be amortized over a period of 48 years.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">We use RSGM for the amortization of (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes to customers. The deferred taxes will be amortized over a period ranging from 46 to 48 years.</link:footnote>
